  "rulings": [
    {"comment":"Skyline Cascade's triggered ability doesn't tap the creature. It can target any creature, tapped or untapped. If that creature is already untapped at the beginning of its controller's next untap step, the effect won't do anything.","oracle_id":"79301ae1-8c9c-4723-be21-dc27e1646f35","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"The triggered ability tracks the creature, but not its controller. If the creature changes controllers before its first controller's next untap step has come around, then it won't untap during its new controller's next untap step.","oracle_id":"79301ae1-8c9c-4723-be21-dc27e1646f35","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"A creature spell that's multiple colors is each of those colors. For example, Ahn-Crop Champion is a white creature and a green creature, so it can benefit from either Oketra's Monument or Rhonas's Monument—or both at once.","oracle_id":"b6294891-79e6-4f2a-a82d-6cffce968356","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Each Monument has one ability that reduces the cost of creature spells of a certain color, and a triggered ability that triggers whenever you cast any creature spell—not just a creature spell of that color.","oracle_id":"b6294891-79e6-4f2a-a82d-6cffce968356","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Each Monument's triggered ability triggers as the creature spell is cast and resolves before that creature spell resolves. The ability will resolve even if that creature spell is countered.","oracle_id":"b6294891-79e6-4f2a-a82d-6cffce968356","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"The triggered ability of Kefnet's Monument doesn't tap the creature. It can target any creature, tapped or untapped. If that creature is already untapped at the beginning of its controller's next untap step, the effect won't do anything.","oracle_id":"b6294891-79e6-4f2a-a82d-6cffce968356","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"To determine the total cost of a creature spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the creature remains unchanged, no matter what the total cost to cast it was.","oracle_id":"b6294891-79e6-4f2a-a82d-6cffce968356","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"cd0d7141-46d2-4aa3-bc77-6b3b4513803e","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},
    {"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}
  ]
}
